<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

  <!--
    Toolbar and status-bar command icons.

    Source: Microsoft Fluent UI System Icons — https://github.com/microsoft/fluentui-system-icons
    Licence: MIT, Copyright (c) 2020 Microsoft Corporation. The full text is kept verbatim at
             assets/licenses/FluentUI-System-Icons-LICENSE.txt.

    Each geometry below is the `d` attribute of the corresponding upstream SVG, copied unmodified;
    the upstream file is named in the comment above it so any icon can be re-derived or refreshed
    without guessing which one it was. Only the icons the toolbar actually uses are vendored — the
    pack itself is not a dependency, and there is no build step: a StreamGeometry resource is the
    whole integration.

    All of them are the *regular* (outline) 24px weight, so the toolbar reads as one set. A PathIcon
    fills with the inherited Foreground, which is what makes these follow the Light/Dark theme
    variant instead of needing a second, hard-coded copy per theme.

    A geometry serves however many commands mean the same thing: the folder-open icon below is both
    File > Open and the status bar's "Open containing folder", and the document-PDF icon is both
    File > Export to PDF and the status bar's "Open exported PDF" — one subject, one glyph, rather
    than the same idea pasted in twice under two names.
  -->

